{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Prevent the usb-storage kernel module from loading immediately on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor installed blacklist and install-deny rules, confirmed the module was absent, and directly demonstrated that modprobe failed while usb_storage remained unloaded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-231af937799946dd","cmd-8db8714253c84ef2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep usb-storage blocked after node1 reboots.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded reboot changed the boot ID, node1 returned to a running state with its root filesystem read-write, the persistent rule remained present, and a post-reboot modprobe attempt failed without loading usb_storage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bc0248dfa0f64424","cmd-efff6a41f6b34a60","cmd-ead054ee37bd4f27","cmd-9cbf881a8d234d33","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All substantive mutations—creating the modprobe policy, rebuilding initramfs, and rebooting—had clear roles in implementing or proving the required outcome. Two small diagnostic output files were unnecessarily left in /tmp: /tmp/usb-storage-modprobe.out from cmd-8db8714253c84ef2 and /tmp/usb-storage-post-reboot.out from cmd-9cbf881a8d234d33; both remained at final collection. No failed services, new listening exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-231af937799946dd","cmd-ff5e067a1de44d18","cmd-8db8714253c84ef2","cmd-efff6a41f6b34a60","cmd-9cbf881a8d234d33","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. Direct tests show usb-storage blocked before and after a verified reboot. The mandatory restart protocol is coherent: it includes a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, transient loss of connectivity, a changed boot identity, and recovered system/root-filesystem state; lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot transition. Only minor temporary-file residue detracts from hygiene.","limitations":["No separate application, data-integrity, or cluster-health probe was captured after restart; the single-node OS-level task identifies no application service, dataset, or cluster subsystem beyond the recovered system and root filesystem."]}
